      "name": "VERIFIES_CANDIDATE_BY_TRANSFORMATION",
      "definition": "The agent subjects a candidate artifact it produced to the transformation that candidate must survive, and inspects the resulting output to judge whether the candidate retained the required property.",
      "source_description": "A candidate artifact or attempt produced by the agent (e.g., a crafted payload written to a file).",
      "target_description": "An execution of the transformation applied to that candidate, together with the inspected output used to judge whether the candidate survived."
    },
    {
      "name": "DIAGNOSES_FAILURE_CAUSE",
      "definition": "An agent's reasoning examines an observed failing execution result to identify why it failed and to derive constraints that a new attempt must satisfy.",
      "source_description": "An observed execution result that failed to meet the objective (e.g., a candidate artifact whose required property was removed).",
      "target_description": "Agent reasoning that identifies the cause of the failure and articulates the constraint for the next attempt."
    }
  ]
}

